Z||000018||frontal lobe||02-14-2001||02:16 PM||||Yeah, Stimpy, now that I have kids and could use a mini-van, and the fact that I've always wanted a mid-engine vehicle, I want to snap up a 4-banger Previa.  Hey, I've always wanted a supercharged engine, too.  Previa has that!  Now to get that 50/50 weight distribution, the 9 year old has to sit with the 5 year old in the back row, wife in the middle, and 8 year old sits up front with me.  Now, when my wife, drives...<P>Just joking around.  I have a friend that has one, and it is wierd to see the 4-banger lying there side-ways under the front floor.<P>Maybe if they had the new nissan in a different color it would look better.  I don't like those vertical strips on the front fascia either.  What is that all about?  I wouldn't mind having one, though.  I could just always approach it from the rear and not look at the front!||||reg||1
Z||000019||ChadMan||02-14-2001||02:26 PM||||With its blunt front end and Audi-copycat gunslit windows, the new Z is butt-ugly in my opinion.  <P>Like Tigger, I thought the previous-generation Z was beautiful (especially for a Japanese sports car).  When I was worked at Mid-Ohio, we had two of them we used as pace cars.  It wasn't often I got to drive them, but when I did, I made the most of it.  300 hp...damn, what a rush.<P>I'd rather have a Fiero with an LT-1, of course.  Like Paul Vargyas's.  Now that's a beautiful car...I'm rambling.  Slow day at work.  Sorry.||||reg||13
