Z||000021||kslish||02-14-2001||04:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>Ya, another egg with wheels. I really liked the looks and performance of the 90s something 300Z twin turbo... and I hate Japanese cars for the most part.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I agree with you 100% Roger about the mid-90's 300Z's.  I had the chance to buy a twin turbo last year for an insanely low price (less then $10,000) with 72,000 miles on it and it ran like a dream.  Owner needed to get rid of it quickly.  It was silver with black leather interior and the 300 or so horsepower that the turbo V6 had sure moved the car like nothing else I've had the chance to drive yet.  I managed to talk myself out of it because I didn't want to put myself into debt and my insurance would have gone literally through the roof...so I went and got myself an '87 GT instead   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 02-14-2001).]||||reg||1
