Z||000024||Will||02-15-2001||10:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>The original Z car had integrated strut towers , makes adjusting the rear struts easy ..We have lots of 240Z racers in our club.<BR>JM</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I hope is has intergrated strut towers. Be in for a might rough ride if it didn't.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>My dad has a '75 280Z with a V8. We weighed it. With him in it it has PERFECT 50/50 weight dist.<P>The idea behind a mid-rear engine car is low moment of inertia, not weight distribution.||||reg||1
Z||000025||Slammed Fiero||02-15-2001||12:06 PM||||A couple of guys in our club always gripe about the weight of their inline SOHC 6's , saying they weigh as much as a small block. Most of them have moved on to different cars now , since there Z's got as fast as they were gonna ever be. I was suprised when the one guy told me his 94 300ZX TT's motor weighed in @ 667lbs!!!! he said there was a lot of nickle in the block and it was built heavy to withstand HP , he is getting 450hp with just a mild rebuild , port polish , factory pistons , stock turbo's and a bit more boost....<P>The 300ZX TT and the 240Z were the best sports cars ever to come out of Japan (IMHO) the RX-7 (last gen) is close , but the guy in our club has had 3 motors in his car so........kaboon ..seals...more turbo ...kaboon ..new seals...DOH!<P>I almost bought a 240Z (71) before I found fiero's.....<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
